{
  "summary": "Mark all database read, write, erase, and transaction operations in WalletBatch as [[nodiscard]]. Update all callers across the wallet subsystem to either handle returned failure codes or explicitly cast them to void with an explanatory comment.",
  "problem": "Wallet database write and erase failures were frequently ignored across the codebase. When database operations fail silently, in-memory state can diverge from persistent on-disk records (such as address indices, transaction records, or address book entries), risking wallet corruption, desynchronization, or data loss.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'A common theme in the wallet is that many database write failures are ignored, when they should probably be handled, or at least documented that a failure is being ignored.'",
    "Commit 8be1f0d8ad note: 'This is the first time we write to this wallet, if there's a write failure now, there will likely be write failures in the future. Better to stop loading the wallet and not let the user use it at this time.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "The diff spans several wallet components (migration, exports, transaction insertion, descriptors, scanning progress), touching error control flow across many call sites.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Its base dependency PR 35752 has merged, removing encryption and passphrase refactors from this PR's diff and leaving only the nodiscard annotations and handling of remaining database writes.",
  "card": "This pull request marks all database interaction methods in WalletBatch as nodiscard and updates callers across the wallet to handle failures or explicitly document ignored errors. Previously, callers frequently ignored write failures silently, allowing in-memory state (such as key generation indices, transaction state updates, and address book metadata) to diverge from persistent disk records without alerting the user. Failure handling now halts or surfaces errors during address generation, loading, wallet export, and wallet migration. The previously required dependency for encryption state updates (#35752) has merged.",
